# THE BUILD CONTEXT IS AN ALLOWLIST: nothing enters the image unless a line
# below lets it back in.
#
# This was a denylist, and a denylist fails open. The repo root collects
# files no list anticipated, and `COPY . .` baked them into every image:
# three Fidelity .har captures (authenticated brokerage traffic -- cookies,
# tokens, account numbers), a 9 MB server.log, the warehouse, agent tool
# directories. Found in a built image in October 2026.
*

# What the image runs.
!cli.py
!pyproject.toml
!requirements*.txt
!engine/
!research/
!server/
!tools/
!fidelity_gateway/
!config/
!web/

# What `cli.py test` reads inside the image (`docker compose run --rm test`).
!conftest.py
!tests/
!docs/
!README.md
!CHANGELOG.md
!CLAUDE.md
!AGENTS.md
!plan.md
!Dockerfile
!docker-compose.yml
!.dockerignore
!.gitignore

# Inside those directories, what must still never enter. Each is git-ignored
# too; listed here so loosening the allowlist cannot let one back in.

# Secrets. Credentials belong only in an env file handed over at runtime
# (engine/core/secrets.py's policy). `.env*` because `.env` and `*.env`
# match neither `.env.staging` nor `.env.production`.
.env
.env*
*.env
**/.env*

# fidelity-api's credential-equivalent files: Fidelity*.json is the
# Playwright storage_state of an AUTHENTICATED brokerage session, and
# fidelity_trace*.zip records .fill() arguments -- the password in
# cleartext. Recon dumps and HAR captures are session traffic. Statements
# and positions are account data.
Fidelity.json
Fidelity_*.json
**/Fidelity*.json
fidelity_trace*.zip
**/fidelity_trace*.zip
**/*.har
.fidelity_recon/
recon_*.json
**/recon_*.json
Statements/
Portfolio_Positions*.csv
**/Portfolio_Positions*.csv
config/fidelity_live.yaml
config/fidelity_local.yaml

# State and data: bind-mounted or volume-mounted at runtime
# (docker-compose.yml), never baked in.
state/
data/
output/
*.db
**/*.db
**/*.db.lock
**/*.duckdb
**/*.parquet
**/*.log

# Version control, caches, build output. The frontend is built in its own
# stage from package.json and the lockfile; a developer node_modules is
# hundreds of MB and the wrong architecture on a cross-build.
.git
**/__pycache__/
**/*.py[cod]
**/.pytest_cache/
**/.ruff_cache/
**/*.egg-info/
web/node_modules/
web/dist/
web/.omo/
